21/Apr/26 1:36 PM;mkuperst;Shifted out per 4/20 email from Stacy Garcia;

As an update, the UMS PDMS PHA is still approaching MRF review. We have been in a holding pattern awaiting NAVSEA technical concurrence on an additional use case of BeCu resulting in an update to HIF PDMS-13; that concurrence is being spearheaded by Lance and is expected by 4/24 at the latest. Therefore, we are anticipating that the planned schedule presented in the email below will shift by two weeks, with EB MRF review expected to begin Monday, May 4{^}th{^} with planned distribution to NAVSEA on Friday, May 8{^}th{^}.

 

I will continue to provide updates as they are available. The next update should be more accurate with regards to the EB review window as the PHA moves into GDMS configuration management. I appreciate your patience and awareness of this upcoming review!;;;

column49:
Per email from Ashley White:

BLUF: 
D422 ESOH has drafted a BOE for the assessment of EMBT blow with ROV deployed, and are looking for engineering inputs on hours needed to perform additional assessments. 

Request:
Each of the following departments (D413, D417, D440, D496, D419, D374) has a box labeled within the BOE-ACTIVITIES tab on the {color:#4c9aff}attached excel{color}. Please list the amount of hours needed in order to perform the necessary engineering assessments that will support characterizing the risk for EMBT blow with ROV deployed. 

{color:#4c9aff}Excel:{color}

{color:#4c9aff}\\us-ct-eb01\EBDepts\Programs.408\D408_ESOH\External_Department_Share\SSW_External_Share\SSW EMBT Blow w_Equipment Deployed\BOE_EST_EMBT_ROV Deployed.xlsm{color}

Background:
D422 ESOH Engineering is inquiring with select departments who took part in the development of an Analysis Completion Summary (ACS) (which is a smaller, more focused safety assessment) for an EMBT Blow with EST deployed. This analysis was developed in 2024 and issued to NAVSEA for approval and HIF acknowledgement in February 2025. We are still waiting for approval with comment (any day now).

This inquiry now is for an ACS for EMBT blow with ROV deployed. {color:#4c9aff}A draft HIF was developed{color} with key stakeholders towards the end of 2025. It was identified that additional engineering efforts would need to be performed in order to determine the associated risk assessment for the hazard, and to further determine appropriate mitigating actions that would support lowering the associated risk. 

{color:#4c9aff}Draft HIF:{color}

{color:#4c9aff}\\us-ct-eb01\EBDepts\Programs.408\D408_ESOH\External_Department_Share\SSW_External_Share\SSW EMBT Blow w_Equipment Deployed\CUI_SSWx8-01DRAFT_10.6.25.docx{color}

BOE INFO:
The single activity captured in the BOE-ACTIVITIES tab is meant to be an LOE that captures the entirety of the hours needed for engineering support prior to development of the ACS. 

The BOE-PRODUCT tab captures the ACS that will be authored by D422 with the support of this engineering community. This product will have the typical ESOH product steps for Document Development, and Engineering Review, so there will be hours allocated there for actual time and input into the analysis. 

Please provide inputs by 4/10/26. If you cannot meet that timeframe, please reach out to me. 
Any question or concerns in general, don’t hesitate to reach out. Thanks!

{color:#4c9aff}Folder:{color}

{color:#4c9aff}\\us-ct-eb01\EBDepts\Programs.408\D408_ESOH\External_Department_Share\SSW_External_Share\SSW EMBT Blow w_Equipment Deployed{color}

Per 3/18/26 email from Stacy Garcia

we’re re-scheduling the GDMS C2S/PDMS FHA face-to-face for the week of March 30{^}th{^} (tentatively April 1{^}st{^} – 2{^}nd{^}). As an unplanned benefit, we now have some extra time to *{color:#4c9aff}review the read-ahead files for the new HIFs that GDMS drafted to support FHA comment adjudication.{color}* I have saved all new HIFs provided by GDMS in the folder linked below for review and commenting. {color:#4c9aff}*Please make comments and edits directly in track changes in preparation for review and discussion of the HIFs during the face-to-face*{color}. As a high-level reminder, these new HIFs were generated as part of the comment adjudication effort in response to EB comments. Therefore, we want to verify that the HIFs satisfy the comments which drove their creation, as well as ensure that we agree with the HIF content as written. Please let me know if you have any questions and look out for forthcoming updates on the rescheduled face-to-face. Thanks!

 

Folder:

{color:#4c9aff}*X:\Programs.408\D408_ESOH\External_Department_Share\SSW_External_Share\SSW UMS C2S PDMS\3.16.26 HIF Files\Track Changes*{color}

